# Shell scripts and systemd units MUST be committed with LF endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows and deployed on Linux. Without this, git's autocrlf turns
# install.sh into CRLF on checkout, and bash then fails on the shebang with
# `/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory` -- an error that names neither the file
# nor the real cause. A systemd unit with CRLF fails more quietly still: it parses, and the
# trailing \r ends up inside ExecStart's path.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.service.in text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
